GIT
===

Version control for your code.


WHAT IT IS
----------
Git tracks every change you make to your files.
Like a time machine for your project.


HOW IT WORKS
------------
1. You work on files
2. You stage changes (git add)
3. You commit (git commit)
4. Git saves a snapshot

Each commit is a checkpoint you can return to.


WHY USE IT
----------
• Undo mistakes easily
• Try new ideas safely
• Work with others
• Keep complete history
• Backup your work


THE BASICS
----------
git init        Start tracking
git add .       Stage all changes
git commit      Save snapshot
git status      See what changed


BRANCHES
--------
Branches let you work on ideas separately.

Main branch:  Your stable code
New branch:   Experiment safely

Switch back and forth without losing work.


REMOTE
------
Push your code to GitHub/GitLab.
Others can download and contribute.


